2	// opc: lint, pack and deploy an OPC package to Multica.
3	//
4	// An OPC package is an Agent Companies v1 package (COMPANY.md, teams/, agents/,
5	// projects/, tasks/, skills/) plus the fgopc extension: workflows/<slug>/WORKFLOW.md
6	// and .fgopc.yaml. See ../spec/package-format.md.
7	//
8	//     opc.mjs lint   <package>
9	//     opc.mjs pack   <package> [-o out.tar.gz]
10	//     opc.mjs plan   <package>                 # what deploy would change, no writes
11	//     opc.mjs deploy <package> [--activate-routines]
12	//
13	// Deploy is idempotent: entities are matched by slug through a state file
14	// (<package>/.opc/multica-<workspace>.json), falling back to name. Secret values
15	// come from environment variables named in .fgopc.yaml and are never printed.
16	//
17	// Environment: MULTICA_API (default http://127.0.0.1:8310), MULTICA_TOKEN_FILE
18	// (default $MULTICA_HOME/.pat, MULTICA_HOME default ~/multica-spike).
19	//
20	// Needs only Node 18+: YAML comes from the vendored js-yaml (vendor/js-yaml.mjs).
